    primitive_receiver_trait_impl_dispatch_2026-08-07, 2, "2026-11-03 lane A: Defect B (pure-Simple resolver) landed 809377f4421 and 311d74eb3e8; spec 6/7 (i32 collapses to i64 impl row still red); Defect A (seed JIT closures_structs.rs:1530) needs seed redeploy; stays open"
    primitive_receiver_trait_impl_dispatch_2026-08-07, 3, "2026-11-10 g100-p1: HIR preserves primitive trait method identities (98731c07158); unit+HIR specs green in interpreter; native verification pending"
    primitive_receiver_trait_impl_dispatch_2026-08-07, 4, "2026-11-26 aarch64 Linux run: admitted aarch64 Stage 2 built from origin/release/1.0.0 76892f19a3a (stage2-sanity pass, sha256 567541f4ffd021a1, cranelift-built); probes built with SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP=1 SIMPLE_NATIVE_GO_TO_END=1 SIMPLE_FILE_WORKERS=0 SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_WHOLE_PROGRAM=1 <stage2> native-build main.spl --backend=<b> --entry-closure. Fixed: single-module b0_e (impl MarkerProbe for text and i64) prints t=1001 w=1002, and impl for i64 plus i32 prints n=1003 w=1002 (no i32->i64 collapse) on llvm and cranelift; a cross-module Marker for i32/i64 prints n=1032 w=1064; seed 11-26 specs primitive_receiver_trait_impl_dispatch 15/15, primitive_method_identity 3/3, primitive_trait_identity_hir 1/1. Still failing: the acceptance fixture test/fixtures/compiler/primitive_trait_identity (copied to a scratch dir) fails MIR lowering on both backends with E-RTI-006: two rows for callee mark in module provider (type:i32::provider.Other::mark), because the RTI callee key used the leaf method name so Marker.mark and Other.mark on i32 collide. The minimal single-file two-traits-on-i32 case fails the same way; a struct does not. Fixed in this branch (return_type_interface_v1.spl key keeps the full method part; new rti_primitive_trait_method_rows_spec 1/3 -> 3/3). Separately, the spec's own in-tree command (--source src/lib --entry test/fixtures/...) stops earlier with missing module surface for provider (source closure of 1 file). Native re-run needs a Stage 2 rebuilt from this branch."
    primitive_receiver_trait_impl_dispatch_2026-08-07, 5, "2026-11-26 correction to the previous line: E-RTI-006 is not the only fixture failure. With go-to-end the same 76892f19a3a build of the fixture also reports, on both backends, provider: ambiguous scalar trait method: mark (Marker default inherited body self.mark() while Other.mark for i32 is also visible) and main: unresolved method call: mark and unresolved method call: inherited (route=runtime-fallback key=::mark, through the SelectedMarker alias / Narrow alias imports). The single-trait cross-module case only hits E-RTI-006. The RTI key fix on this branch removes one of three error classes; trait-scoped scalar dispatch inside default bodies and alias-imported scalar trait calls remain. Status -> open."
    primitive_receiver_trait_impl_dispatch_2026-08-07, 6, "2026-11-27 P1-1: Fixed pure-Simple HIR+MIR scalar trait dispatch parity (trait default self.m TraitMethod provenance, sibling Visibility.Package filtering in mir_visible_scalar_traits_v1, trait-scoped+inherent scalar MIR keys & literal receiver recovery, non-nominal match-continue guards). Verified primitive_trait_identity_mir_spec 2/2, primitive_method_identity 3/3, primitive_trait_identity_hir 1/1, scalar_trait_visibility 2/2, rti_primitive_trait_method_rows 3/3, primitive_receiver_trait_impl_dispatch 15/15 on Windows interpreter. waiting-for: Linux Stage-2 native LLVM rebuild and test/03_system/compiler/primitive_trait_identity_native_spec.spl."

